uç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#Determining the effective factors in predicting diet adherence using an intelligent model#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/TPCIRV65","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WIXNTIHY?page=1&annotation=D9CCKXRR","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WIXNTIHY?page=1&annotation=DTCPTS4X","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WIXNTIHY?page=1&annotation=GJ99L8D8","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Determining the effective factors in predicting diet adherence using an intelligent model","Authors":"Hediye Mousavi, Majid Karandish, Amir Jamshidnezhad, Ali Mohammad Hadianfard","Year":2022,"DOI":"10.1038/s41598-022-16680-8","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"This study aimed to predict adherence to the prescribed diets using a hybrid model of artificial neural networks (ANNs) and the genetic algorithm (GA). In this study, 26 factors affecting diet adherence were modeled using ANN and GA(ANGA)","Findings":"The results showed that the accuracy of the proposed ANN and ANGA models for predicting diet adherence was 93.22% and 93.51%, respectively.","Conclusions":"Therefore, applying the proposed model can help dietitians identify people who need more support to adhere to the diet.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"4bzihh","at":1774939750924},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/mousaviDeterminingEffectiveFactors2022a.md"},
